# Design Contract

Use the pinned DenchCo visual adapter as the baseline, then record only deliberate target-specific token and interaction decisions here. Navigation and synthesis must follow the target's audience and governing question.

Every displayed governing-question callout must expose the `governing-question` marker and use the active accent colour for both its inline-start rail and question text at every supported viewport. Ordinary quotations remain neutral.

When the Human Wiki uses Mermaid, adapt the pinned semantic diagram roles (`kb-source`, `kb-evidence`, `kb-snapshot`, `kb-normative`, `kb-canonical`, `kb-product`, `kb-derived`, `kb-consumer`, and `kb-verification`) through the complete renderer dependency closure. Use the target accent family, preserve accessible titles and descriptions, distinguish derived surfaces from authority, and verify the complete topology at desktop, tablet, and mobile widths.
